# AGENTS.md — `results/`

Root [`../AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) applies. All payloads here are pipeline-owned
and must match the root [`README.md`](../README.md) contract.

- Never hand-edit a result, even for a cosmetic fix. Change code/config and
  rebuild the declared target.
- Do not commit generated results regardless of size. A delivery freezes exact
  outputs under `reporting/` with provenance; it does not make `results/` source.
- Write only declared outputs. QC goes to `results/qc/`, data-derived figures to
  `results/figures/`, terminal report tables to `results/tables/`, and declared
  execution logs to `results/logs/`.
- Reusable downstream datasets belong in `data/processed/`.
- Agents may run the pipeline and produce `results/provenance.json`. They may not
  register/archive the run without explicit user approval.
- Before completion, confirm generated files are ignored and no result payload
  is staged in Git.
